{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788970501,"nonce":"x4QOm+mhIBYdVGkS7Si2rakQoKk=","title":"ability-cast verb: no pawn ability or psycast can be fired","message":"Nothing in the 139 verbs can cast a `Pawn` ability. `Pawn_AbilityTracker` is unreachable: an ability a pawn HAS cannot be used, so psycasts, Royalty abilities and every modded `AbilityDef` on this bench are inert.\n\nPaired with the `use` verb (`d318d4a`), which is how a pawn LEARNS most of them — a psytrainer is `CompUseEffect_LearnAbility` and a psylink level is `PsychicAmplifier`. Learning without casting is half a feature; this is the other half.\n\n## What is out of reach on this bench\n\n`dorian.fingerkill` ships three psycasts, all `ParentName=\"PsycastBase\"`, `Verb_CastPsycast`, and all three are orderable from Dad's catalog as psytrainers:\n\n- **Bloodbond** — level 5, `Ability_PsyfocusCost` 0.30, `Ability_EntropyGain` 20, range 24.9, requires line of sight, targets pawns only, `hostile:False`, `displayGizmoWhileUndrafted:True`. Comp `Fingerkill.CompAbilityEffect_Bloodbond`.\n- **Fingerkill** — level 6, psyfocus 0.01, entropy 0, **range 9999, `requireLineOfSight:False`**, targets pawns and animals, `hostile:True`. Comp `Fingerkill.CompAbilityEffect_Fingerkill`.\n- **Voidpull** — same family.\n\nPlus the 29 vanilla Royalty psytrainers in the catalog.\n\n## The gate to reproduce\n\nThe player's route is `Ability.GetGizmo()` -\u003e `Command_Ability` -\u003e click -\u003e `Ability.QueueCastingJob(LocalTargetInfo target, LocalTargetInfo destination)`. The preconditions to re-implement and cite, all of them widget-side:\n\n- `Ability.CanCast` and `Ability.GizmoDisabled(out string reason)` — the disabled reason the player is shown.\n- `Ability.Verb.CanHitTarget(target)` plus `verbProperties.targetParams` (`canTargetPawns`, `canTargetSelf`, `canTargetAnimals`, `canTargetMechs`, `canTargetBuildings`, `canTargetLocations`) and `requireLineOfSight`/`range`.\n- For a psycast: `AbilityDef.level` against `pawn.psychicEntropy`'s psylink level, `Ability_PsyfocusCost` against current psyfocus, and `Ability_EntropyGain` against `Pawn_PsychicEntropyTracker` headroom (`WouldOverflowEntropy`). These are three separate refusals and must not be collapsed into one.\n- Per-comp: `CompAbilityEffect.CanApplyOn(target, dest)` and `.Valid(target, throwMessages)` — a modded comp can refuse for reasons the base verb knows nothing about, which is exactly the Fingerkill/Bloodbond case.\n- Cooldown: `Ability.CooldownTicksRemaining`.\n\n**Do not bypass any of these.** DESIGN's action model: a player verb re-implements its precondition and cites it by file and member; `dev:*` may bypass, a player verb may not.\n\n## Open question for the scoping pass\n\nWhether the read half is a separate verb (`abilities {pawn}` listing what a pawn has, each with its gates evaluated and a `castable` verdict) or a section on `pawn`. The agent cannot choose a target without it either way, so one of the two must ship with this.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `abilities {pawn}` (or `pawn {sections:[\"abilities\"]}`) lists every ability the pawn has with `def`, `label`, `level`, `psyfocus_cost`, `entropy_gain`, `range`, `requires_los`, `cooldown_ticks_remaining`, `castable` and, when not castable, the reason in the game's own vocabulary.\n- `ability-cast {pawn, ability, target}` queues the cast through `Ability.QueueCastingJob`, never by invoking the comp directly.\n- Every refusal above is reachable and distinct: insufficient psylink level, insufficient psyfocus, entropy overflow, out of range, no line of sight, wrong target type, on cooldown, comp refusal. Each names its member.\n- A target argument accepts a pawn id and a cell, and refuses a cell for an ability whose `targetParams.canTargetLocations` is false.\n- Casting Bloodbond on a prisoner produces the bond hediff on the target and the murderous-rage mental state the def describes; casting Fingerkill destroys the target's heart and takes the caster's next body part in the mod's fixed sequence.\n- A pawn with no psylink refuses every psycast with the level reason, not with a null dereference.","files":null}]}